  "section_notes": "The final text sets the S2 permanent failure ceiling at 8% rather than 5%, with the 5% level reduced to a regulator benchmark, which is the main gain for Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). S3 gives a 6-year retrofit window, which favours Northwind's low shut-off coverage, while S4 delays built-in suppression to 36 months, which favours Halcyon's cost position. S5 keeps the 8-per-100,000 mandatory recall trigger, which would apply to Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9), but it allows regulator-approved resumption after corrective action."
